<Layout title="For parents | Kin & Campus" description="Enroll your student in a young adult wellness program in Blacksburg. A board-certified pediatrician holds refills, sick days, forms, and the year, with you in the loop by agreement.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">For parents</div><h1>Enroll them in a year they can grow in.</h1><p class="lead">Kin &amp; Campus is a young adult wellness program in Blacksburg, led by a board-certified pediatrician who lives here. Enrollment is how they spend the college years with a doctor who already knows the plan, a calendar that follows campus life, and a way of growing into care they will use long after they leave town.</p></div>
<div class="w"><img class="photo" src={href("photos/arch-fall.jpg")} width="678" height="452" alt="A stone arch on campus under fall trees">

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:48px">Before they join</div>
<h2>A few things to settle as they enroll.</h2>
<p class="lead">This is what we walk through with families in the last stretch of summer. The AAP says much of the same, and so does Virginia Tech's paperwork.</p>
<ol class="steps">
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div><h3>Name the program in town</h3><p>Know who will hold the year before the first fever. We start with a visit and the plan their hometown doctor already has.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div><h3>Move the prescriptions</h3><p>Start with ADHD. Campus clinics often cannot continue those medications. Anxiety and depression prescriptions that began at home need a local doctor too.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div><h3>Sign the immunization form</h3><p>Virginia Tech wants it in the Healthy Hokies portal, signed by a clinician. Do not leave this for move-in weekend.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div><h3>Housing letter, if they need one</h3><p>SSD handles air conditioning, a single room, and the rest. They will ask for a letter from a doctor who knows the student.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div><h3>Decide what we may share</h3><p>At 18 the chart is theirs. We write down what they want you to hear. Then we follow it. Belonging includes an agreement, not a guess.</p></div></li>
</ol>
<p class="cite"><a href="https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/young-adult/Pages/Healthy-Tips-for-the-College-Freshman.aspx">AAP college checklist</a>. <a href="https://healthcenter.vt.edu/new_student/required_immunizations.html">VT immunizations</a>. <a href="https://ssd.vt.edu/access/housing.html">VT SSD housing</a>.</p>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">While they are here</div>
<h2>What the program holds through the year.</h2>
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Refills</h3><p>ADHD, anxiety, depression, asthma, thyroid. Whatever they already take. We keep it going and copy the hometown doctor when something changes.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Sick days</h3><p>Someone in town who already knows their baseline. During the school year we can usually see them the same week, and often the same day.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Forms</h3><p>Immunizations, SSD housing, club and sports physicals. The paperwork that otherwise sits in a group text until it is late.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Who we tell</h3><p>The rule you agree on together. If the plan changes, their hometown doctor gets a note that afternoon.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">Why families enroll</div>
<p class="lead">Forty-four percent of college students report at least one listed mental-health diagnosis. Those conditions do not pause for freshman year, which is why a program that lasts the year matters more than a single visit.</p>
<p class="cite" style="margin-bottom:20px">ACHA-NCHA III, Fall 2024. 33,763 students at 48 U.S. schools. <a href="https://www.acha.org/wp-content/uploads/NCHA-IIIb_FALL_2024_REFERENCE_GROUP_EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.pdf">Executive summary (PDF)</a>.</p>
<p>An ER visit can cost hundreds of dollars, or several thousand on a high-deductible plan. If it is a true emergency, call 911. For the rest of the year, start with a doctor who already knows them.</p>
<p class="cite">Large-employer plans averaged $646 out of pocket. <a href="https://www.kff.org/health-costs/emergency-department-visits-exceed-affordability-threshold-for-many-consumers-with-private-insurance/">KFF / Peterson-Kaiser</a>, 2019 claims (published 2022).</p>

<div style="margin-top:48px"><h2>When you are ready to enroll, we will talk.</h2><p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:28px">A short call first, about the program and the year. Then they meet us in town.</p>
<p><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Join the program</a> &nbsp; <a class="lnk" href={href("membership")}>What membership includes &rarr;</a></p></div>
</div>
